{
 "caveats": [
  "The pre look date is an estimate: first_seen_utc minus the stored pre_lag p50 or p90, then converted to WIT. It is not the date of a scene; individual pixels sit on both sides of it.",
  "The direction comparison uses WIT days. The pre look instant is anchored on first_seen_utc, then shifted to WIT; acq_date is already a WIT local day and is not shifted again; the prior cutoff is the first_seen_wit day.",
  "A prior detection makes contamination possible, not established: a VIIRS pixel locates a thermal anomaly, not a perimeter.",
  "changed_ha is the published Task 18 figure. Nothing here recomputes, corrects, or ranks it, and the two directions are never added together.",
  "no_prior_detection means no prior detection strictly before the estimated pre look. A detection exactly on the pre look date is neither before nor after and falls in this group; its count and date are still reported.",
  "Recurrence distance is centroid-to-site. Whether the footprint comes within recurrence.radius_m is computed from the member circles, not the centroid. recurrent_share is read from events.json and is not reconciled with the distance.",
  "The 8 assessed entries with status no local reference have no lag fields and no direction; they are listed separately, not dropped.",
  "p50 and p90 are separate estimates. When they disagree, both directions are reported and the event is not resolved to one."
 ],
